Description: RMX mode - drum pads and rolls in time with the master deck
 A few of the RMX-1000's X-PAD tricks for the skin's RMX panel: four drum
 pads (KICK, SNARE, CLAP, HAT) on the master and in the headphones. A tap
 plays one hit at once; holding a pad rolls it at the ROLL rate (1/1 to
 1/16 of a beat, or 1 SHOT for no roll), with every roll step on the exact
 sample of the grid line of the master deck (the deck that started playing
 most recently; with nothing playing the drums run on at the last tempo).
 BUILD plays a two-bar snare roll that speeds up and gets louder into the
 drop, starting on the next beat.
 .
 New EngineRmx (src/engine/enginermx.{h,cpp}), owned by EngineMixer and run
 once per callback after the decks, so their beat_distance is the one for
 this buffer. The drums are synthesised sample by sample (a pitch-swept
 sine kick, head plus high-passed noise snare, band-passed noise bursts
 for the clap, high-passed noise hat), so there are no sample files to ship
 and nothing depends on the sample rate. A retriggered pad fades its last
 hit out over 3 ms, so fast rolls do not click. The buffer is added to the
 main mix after the crossfader buses, and to the headphones at the cue
 share (the master share arrives with the main mix), so they are always in
 the headphones, whatever the CUE buttons and HEADPHONES MIX - for quiet
 practice with the master turned down.
 .
 While [Pioneered],rmx_mode is on, MidiController hands the DDJ-400's BEAT
 FX section to EngineRmx::handleMidi() before the mapping sees it: BEAT <
 KICK, BEAT > SNARE, FX SELECT CLAP, ON/OFF HAT, SHIFT + ON/OFF BUILD,
 LEVEL/DEPTH the roll rate (so it can be swept while a pad is held), SHIFT +
 LEVEL/DEPTH the drum level. This is in C++ rather than in
 Pioneer-DDJ-400-script.js because a stale user copy of the mapping shadows
 the shipped script (see browse-encoder-zoom.patch). With RMX closed the
 buttons go to the mapping, and the Beat FX, as before.
 .
 Controls, all [Pioneered]: rmx_mode, rmx_pad1..4 (push), rmx_pad1..4_hit
 (flashes on every hit), rmx_rate (0..5) and rmx_rate_0..5 (radio buttons),
 rmx_level (0..100) with rmx_level_down / rmx_level_up, rmx_build, and the
 read-only rmx_deck, rmx_bpm and rmx_beat for the panel's header.
